{"id":"mahabharata-5-080","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":80,"title":"अशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 80 · Draupadi's plea and Krishna's vow","summary":{"en":"Draupadi, weeping, reminds Krishna of how she was dragged by her hair into the assembly while her husbands looked on, and holding up her long black tresses she says that if the Pandavas want peace her old father and brothers and her sons will fight. Krishna promises her that she will see the Kaurava women weeping and her enemies slain, and that his word will not fail.","kn":"ಪತಿಗಳು ನೋಡುತ್ತಿರುವಾಗ ತನ್ನನ್ನು ಕೂದಲು ಹಿಡಿದು ಸಭೆಗೆ ಎಳೆದದ್ದನ್ನು ಅಳುತ್ತಾ ನೆನಪಿಸಿ, ತನ್ನ ಉದ್ದ ಕಪ್ಪು ಕೂದಲನ್ನು ಎತ್ತಿ ಹಿಡಿದು ಪಾಂಡವರು ಶಾಂತಿ ಬಯಸಿದರೆ ವೃದ್ಧ ತಂದೆ, ಸಹೋದರರು, ಮಕ್ಕಳು ಹೋರಾಡುವರು ಎಂದು ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಕೌರವಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರು ಅಳುವುದನ್ನೂ ಶತ್ರುಗಳು ಹತರಾಗುವುದನ್ನೂ ಕಾಣುವೆ, ತನ್ನ ಮಾತು ಸುಳ್ಳಾಗದು ಎಂದು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ವಾಗ್ದಾನ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"द्रौपदी रोते हुए श्रीकृष्ण को याद दिलाती हैं कि कैसे पतियों के देखते उन्हें बाल पकड़कर सभा में घसीटा गया, और अपने लम्बे काले केश उठाकर कहती हैं कि यदि पाण्डव शान्ति चाहते हैं तो उनके वृद्ध पिता, भाई और पुत्र लड़ेंगे। श्रीकृष्ण वचन देते हैं कि वे कौरव स्त्रियों को रोते और अपने शत्रुओं को मरा देखेंगी, और उनका वचन मिथ्या नहीं होगा।","te":"భర్తలు చూస్తుండగా తనను జుట్టు పట్టి సభకు ఈడ్చుకువచ్చిన తీరును ఏడుస్తూ గుర్తుచేసి, తన పొడవైన నల్లని కురులను ఎత్తిపట్టి పాండవులు శాంతి కోరితే వృద్ధుడైన తండ్రి, సోదరులు, కుమారులు పోరాడతారని ద్రౌపది అంటుంది. కౌరవస్త్రీలు ఏడవడం, శత్రువులు హతులవడం చూస్తావని, తన మాట వ్యర్థం కాదని శ్రీకృష్ణుడు ఆమెకు వాగ్దానం చేస్తాడు.","ta":"கணவர்கள் பார்த்திருக்கத் தன்னைக் கூந்தலைப் பற்றிச் சபைக்கு இழுத்து வந்ததை அழுதபடி நினைவூட்டி, தன் நீண்ட கருங்கூந்தலை உயர்த்திப் பிடித்து, பாண்டவர்கள் அமைதியை விரும்பினால் முதிய தந்தையும் சகோதரர்களும் மைந்தர்களும் போரிடுவார்கள் என்று திரௌபதி சொல்கிறாள். கௌரவப் பெண்கள் அழுவதையும் பகைவர் கொல்லப்படுவதையும் காண்பாய், என் சொல் பொய்க்காது என்று ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் வாக்களிக்கிறார்.","ml":"കരഞ്ഞുകൊണ്ട് ദ്രൗപദി, ഭർത്താക്കന്മാർ നോക്കിനിൽക്കെ മുടിക്കു പിടിച്ച് സഭയിലേക്ക് വലിച്ചിഴച്ച അപമാനം കൃഷ്ണനെ ഓർമ്മിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. നീളമുള്ള കറുത്ത മുടി ഉയർത്തിക്കാട്ടി, പാണ്ഡവർ സമാധാനം ആഗ്രഹിച്ചാലും വൃദ്ധനായ പിതാവും സഹോദരന്മാരും മക്കളും പൊരുതുമെന്ന് അവൾ പറയുന്നു. കൗരവ സ്ത്രീകൾ കരയുന്നത് താൻ കാണുമെന്നും ശത്രുക്കൾ വധിക്കപ്പെടുമെന്നും, തന്റെ വാക്ക് പിഴക്കില്ലെന്നും കൃഷ്ണൻ അവൾക്ക് വാക്കുനൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.80; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"राज्ञस्तु वचनं श्रुत्वा धर्मार्थसहितं हितम् ।\nकृष्णा दाशार्हमासीनमब्रवीच्छोककर्षिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard the king's beneficial words, full of dharma and profit, Krishna, tormented by grief, spoke to Dasharha as he sat there."}},{"n":2,"text":"सुता द्रुपदराजस्य स्वसितायतमूर्धजा ।\nसंपूज्य सहदेवं च सात्यकिं च महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The daughter of King Drupada, her dark hair long and glossy, having honored Sahadeva and the great chariot-warrior Satyaki,"}},{"n":3,"text":"भीमसेनं च संशान्तं दृष्ट्वा परमदुर्मनाः ।\nअश्रुपूर्णेक्षणा वाक्यमुवाचेदं मनस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"and seeing Bhimasena calmed, was deeply distressed; the high-minded woman, her eyes full of tears, spoke these words."}},{"n":4,"text":"विदितं ते महाबाहो धर्मज्ञ मधुसूदन ।\nयथा निकृतिमास्थाय भ्रंशिताः पाण्डवाः सुखात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty-armed Madhusudana, knower of dharma, you know how the Pandavas were cast from happiness by deceit."}},{"n":5,"text":"धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्रेण सामात्येन जनार्दन ।\nयथा च संजयो राज्ञा मन्त्रं रहसि श्रावितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know also, Janardana, how Dhritarashtra's son with his ministers had Sanjaya told the king's counsel in private."}},{"n":6,"text":"युधिष्ठिरेण दाशार्ह तच्चापि विदितं तव ।\nयथोक्तः संजयश्चैव तच्च सर्वं श्रुतं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"And, Dasharha, you know what Yudhishthira said to Sanjaya; you have heard all that."}},{"n":7,"text":"पञ्च नस्तात दीयन्तां ग्रामा इति महाद्युते ।\nकुशस्थलं वृकस्थलमासन्दी वारणावतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radiant one, he said: give us five villages, dear sir: Kushasthala, Vrikasthala, Asandi, Varanavata,"}},{"n":8,"text":"अवसानं महाबाहो किंचिदेव तु पञ्चमम् ।\nइति दुर्योधनो वाच्यः सुहृदश्चास्य केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"and, mighty-armed one, any fifth one. Keshava, this is what must be said to Duryodhana and his friends."}},{"n":9,"text":"तच्चापि नाकरोद्वाक्यं श्रुत्वा कृष्ण सुयोधनः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्य दाशार्ह ह्रीमतः संधिमिच्छतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet even this, Krishna, Suyodhana would not do, though he heard the words of modest Yudhishthira, who wished for peace."}},{"n":10,"text":"अप्रदानेन राज्यस्य यदि कृष्ण सुयोधनः ।\nसंधिमिच्छेन्न कर्तव्यस्तत्र गत्वा कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, Krishna, Suyodhana wants a treaty only by refusing to give any kingdom, then do not go there to make one on any account."}},{"n":11,"text":"शक्ष्यन्ति हि महाबाहो पाण्डवाः सृञ्जयैः सह ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रबलं घोरं क्रुद्धं प्रतिसमासितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the Pandavas, mighty-armed one, with the Srinjayas will be able to stand against the Dhartarashtra army, fierce and angry."}},{"n":12,"text":"न हि साम्ना न दानेन शक्योऽर्थस्तेषु कश्चन ।\nतस्मात्तेषु न कर्तव्या कृपा ते मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"No aim with them can be won by conciliation or gifts; therefore, Madhusudana, show them no pity."}},{"n":13,"text":"साम्ना दानेन वा कृष्ण ये न शाम्यन्ति शत्रवः ।\nमोक्तव्यस्तेषु दण्डः स्याज्जीवितं परिरक्षता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, against enemies who are not calmed by conciliation or gifts, the rod of punishment must be used by one who guards his life."}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्मात्तेषु महादण्डः क्षेप्तव्यः क्षिप्रमच्युत ।\nत्वया चैव महाबाहो पाण्डवैः सह सृञ्जयैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, Achyuta, a great punishment should swiftly be hurled at them, by you and by the Pandavas with the Srinjayas, mighty-armed one."}},{"n":15,"text":"एतत्समर्थं पार्थानां तव चैव यशस्करम् ।\nक्रियमाणं भवेत्कृष्ण क्षत्रस्य च सुखावहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This would benefit the Parthas, bring you fame, Krishna, and bring happiness to the kshatriya order."}},{"n":16,"text":"क्षत्रियेण हि हन्तव्यः क्षत्रियो लोभमास्थितः ।\nअक्षत्रियो वा दाशार्ह स्वधर्ममनुतिष्ठता ॥","meaning":{"en":"A kshatriya who has fallen into greed must be killed by a kshatriya, or even by a non-kshatriya, Dasharha, who follows his own dharma."}},{"n":17,"text":"अन्यत्र ब्राह्मणात्तात सर्वपापेष्ववस्थितात् ।\nगुरुर्हि सर्ववर्णानां ब्राह्मणः प्रसृताग्रभुक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Except a brahmana, dear one, even if he is steeped in every sin; for the brahmana is the teacher of all classes and eats first of the offerings."}},{"n":18,"text":"यथावध्ये भवेद्दोषो वध्यमाने जनार्दन ।\nस वध्यस्यावधे दृष्ट इति धर्मविदो विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The knowers of dharma say that the fault that would come from killing one who must not be killed also comes from not killing one who must be killed."}},{"n":19,"text":"यथा त्वां न स्पृशेदेष दोषः कृष्ण तथा कुरु ।\nपाण्डवैः सह दाशार्ह सृञ्जयैश्च ससैनिकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So act, Krishna, that this fault does not touch you, together with the Pandavas and the Srinjayas and their soldiers."}},{"n":20,"text":"पुनरुक्तं च वक्ष्यामि विश्रम्भेण जनार्दन ।\nका नु सीमन्तिनी मादृक्पृथिव्यामस्ति केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall say it again in trust, Janardana: what woman on earth is there like me, Keshava?"}},{"n":21,"text":"सुता द्रुपदराजस्य वेदिमध्यात्समुत्थिता ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नस्य भगिनी तव कृष्ण प्रिया सखी ॥","meaning":{"en":"I rose from the middle of the sacrificial altar, daughter of King Drupada, sister of Dhrishtadyumna, and, Krishna, your dear friend."}},{"n":22,"text":"आजमीढकुलं प्राप्ता स्नुषा पाण्डोर्महात्मनः ।\nमहिषी पाण्डुपुत्राणां पञ्चेन्द्रसमवर्चसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I came into the house of Ajamidha as daughter-in-law of great Pandu, and am the queen of the five Pandavas, each radiant as Indra."}},{"n":23,"text":"सुता मे पञ्चभिर्वीरैः पञ्च जाता महारथाः ।\nअभिमन्युर्यथा कृष्ण तथा ते तव धर्मतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, by the five heroes I bore five sons, great chariot-warriors; as Abhimanyu is to you, so are they to you by dharma."}},{"n":24,"text":"साहं केशग्रहं प्राप्ता परिक्लिष्टा सभां गता ।\nपश्यतां पाण्डुपुत्राणां त्वयि जीवति केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet I was dragged by the hair and tormented in the assembly, in the sight of the Pandavas, while you lived, Keshava."}},{"n":25,"text":"जीवत्सु कौरवेयेषु पाञ्चालेष्वथ वृष्णिषु ।\nदासीभूतास्मि पापानां सभामध्ये व्यवस्थिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the Kauravas, Panchalas and Vrishnis lived, I stood in the midst of the hall made a slave of sinners."}},{"n":26,"text":"निरामर्षेष्वचेष्टेषु प्रेक्षमाणेषु पाण्डुषु ।\nत्राहि मामिति गोविन्द मनसा काङ्क्षितोऽसि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the Pandavas looked on, powerless and unmoving, I longed for you in my heart, Govinda, saying: save me."}},{"n":27,"text":"यत्र मां भगवान्राजा श्वशुरो वाक्यमब्रवीत् ।\nवरं वृणीष्व पाञ्चालि वरार्हासि मतासि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the revered king, my father-in-law, said to me: choose a boon, Panchali; you are fit to receive one."}},{"n":28,"text":"अदासाः पाण्डवाः सन्तु सरथाः सायुधा इति ।\nमयोक्ते यत्र निर्मुक्ता वनवासाय केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I said: let the Pandavas be free, with their chariots and weapons, Keshava, they were released to go to the forest."}},{"n":29,"text":"एवंविधानां दुःखानामभिज्ञोऽसि जनार्दन ।\nत्राहि मां पुण्डरीकाक्ष सभर्तृज्ञातिबान्धवाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, Janardana, know such sorrows; lotus-eyed one, save me with my husbands, kin and relatives."}},{"n":30,"text":"नन्वहं कृष्ण भीष्मस्य धृतराष्ट्रस्य चोभयोः ।\nस्नुषा भवामि धर्मेण साहं दासीकृताभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, by dharma I am the daughter-in-law of both Bhishma and Dhritarashtra, yet I was made a slave."}},{"n":31,"text":"धिग्बलं भीमसेनस्य धिक्पार्थस्य धनुष्मताम् ।\nयत्र दुर्योधनः कृष्ण मुहूर्तमपि जीवति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shame on Bhimasena's strength and on Partha's bow-skill, Krishna, when Duryodhana lives even a moment."}},{"n":32,"text":"यदि तेऽहमनुग्राह्या यदि तेऽस्ति कृपा मयि ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रेषु वै कोपः सर्वः कृष्ण विधीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you would show me favor, if you have pity for me, Krishna, let all your anger be turned upon the Dhartarashtras."}},{"n":33,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा मृदुसंहारं वृजिनाग्रं सुदर्शनम् ।\nसुनीलमसितापाङ्गी पुण्यगन्धाधिवासितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the dark-eyed Draupadi took in her left hand her hair, soft at its ends, curled at its tips, handsome, deep black and perfumed with sweet fragrance,"}},{"n":34,"text":"सर्वलक्षणसंपन्नं महाभुजगवर्चसम् ।\nकेशपक्षं वरारोहा गृह्य सव्येन पाणिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"bearing every auspicious mark, gleaming like a great serpent; the fair-hipped, lotus-eyed woman of elephant gait"}},{"n":35,"text":"पद्माक्षी पुण्डरीकाक्षमुपेत्य गजगामिनी ।\nअश्रुपूर्णेक्षणा कृष्णा कृष्णं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"came to lotus-eyed Krishna, her eyes full of tears, and the dark lady spoke to Krishna."}},{"n":36,"text":"अयं ते पुण्डरीकाक्ष दुःशासनकरोद्धृतः ।\nस्मर्तव्यः सर्वकालेषु परेषां संधिमिच्छता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lotus-eyed one, this hair was seized by Duhshasana's hand; it must be remembered at all times, when you seek peace with the enemy."}},{"n":37,"text":"यदि भीमार्जुनौ कृष्ण कृपणौ संधिकामुकौ ।\nपिता मे योत्स्यते वृद्धः सह पुत्रैर्महारथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If Bhima and Arjuna, Krishna, being wretched, want peace, my aged father will fight with his sons, great chariot-warriors."}},{"n":38,"text":"पञ्च चैव महावीर्याः पुत्रा मे मधुसूदन ।\nअभिमन्युं पुरस्कृत्य योत्स्यन्ति कुरुभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"And my five mighty sons, Madhusudana, will fight the Kurus with Abhimanyu at their head."}},{"n":39,"text":"दुःशासनभुजं श्यामं संछिन्नं पांसुगुण्ठितम् ।\nयद्यहं तं न पश्यामि का शान्तिर्हृदयस्य मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I do not see Duhshasana's dark arm severed and covered in dust, what peace can my heart have?"}},{"n":40,"text":"त्रयोदश हि वर्षाणि प्रतीक्षन्त्या गतानि मे ।\nनिधाय हृदये मन्युं प्रदीप्तमिव पावकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thirteen years have passed while I waited, keeping my anger in my heart like a blazing fire."}},{"n":41,"text":"विदीर्यते मे हृदयं भीमवाक्शल्यपीडितम् ।\nयोऽयमद्य महाबाहुर्धर्मं समनुपश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"My heart is split, pierced by the dart of Bhima's words, now that this mighty-armed man looks only to dharma."}},{"n":42,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा बाष्पसन्नेन कण्ठेनायतलोचना ।\nरुरोद कृष्णा सोत्कम्पं सस्वरं बाष्पगद्गदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So saying, long-eyed Krishna, her throat choked with tears, wept trembling, her voice thick with sobs."}},{"n":43,"text":"स्तनौ पीनायतश्रोणी सहितावभिवर्षती ।\nद्रवीभूतमिवात्युष्णमुत्सृजद्वारि नेत्रजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Her full breasts and broad hips shaking, she shed a stream of tears from her eyes, hot as if melted."}},{"n":44,"text":"तामुवाच महाबाहुः केशवः परिसान्त्वयन् ।\nअचिराद्द्रक्ष्यसे कृष्णे रुदतीर्भरतस्त्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty-armed Keshava comforted her: you will soon see the Bharata women weeping, Krishna."}},{"n":45,"text":"एवं ता भीरु रोत्स्यन्ति निहतज्ञातिबान्धवाः ।\nहतमित्रा हतबला येषां क्रुद्धासि भामिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Timid lady, they will weep so, with their kin and relatives slain, their friends and armies lost, those with whom you are angry."}},{"n":46,"text":"अहं च तत्करिष्यामि भीमार्जुनयमैः सह ।\nयुधिष्ठिरनियोगेन दैवाच्च विधिनिर्मितात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall do that, with Bhima, Arjuna and the twins, by Yudhishthira's command and by fate as ordained."}},{"n":47,"text":"धार्तराष्ट्राः कालपक्वा न चेच्छृण्वन्ति मे वचः ।\nशेष्यन्ते निहता भूमौ श्वशृगालादनीकृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the Dhartarashtras, ripe for destruction, do not heed my words, they will lie slain on the ground, devoured by dogs and jackals."}},{"n":48,"text":"चलेद्धि हिमवाञ्शैलो मेदिनी शतधा भवेत् ।\nद्यौः पतेच्च सनक्षत्रा न मे मोघं वचो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Himalaya might move, the earth might split in a hundred pieces, the sky with its stars might fall, but my word will not be in vain."}},{"n":49,"text":"सत्यं ते प्रतिजानामि कृष्णे बाष्पो निगृह्यताम् ।\nहतामित्राञ्श्रिया युक्तानचिराद्द्रक्ष्यसे पतीन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I promise you truly, Krishna: hold back your tears. You will soon see your husbands with their enemies slain and endowed with glory."}}]}]}